            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-47",
                    "linecount": 55,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 813.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nEFFECT: comp_ssl_g384_bus_vca\nSOURCE: Thompson & Heilemann (DAFx-2026, \"Evaluating Dynamic Range Compressor\n        Models Using Control-Voltage Measurements: An Approach and Dataset\",\n        Sections 3 & 4.1)\nTYPE:   Stereo SSL Logic FX G384 / 4000 G-Series Bus VCA Compressor with\n        Ratio-Dependent Knee, Dual-Pole AUTO Release & THAT 202 VCA Harmonics\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\n--------\nModels the Solid State Logic G384 / 4000 G stereo bus compressor. Features a\nshared stereo peak-sensing sidechain VCA (DBX 2151) with a ratio-dependent static\ncompression knee (wide/gentle at 2:1, progressively tighter toward 10:1), a\nvariable sidechain high-pass filter, the signature two-pole dual-time-constant\nSSL AUTO release circuit, and THAT 202 audio-path VCA harmonic coloration.\n\nPARAMETERS (10 total)\n---------------------\n1. input_gain_db   [-24.0 .. +36.0 dB, default: 0.0]\n   Input trim, a plain gain stage ahead of the sidechain tap. Raising it feeds\n   more level into the existing compressor (so it compresses harder, as on real\n   hardware); it does not alter any other setting.\n\n2. thresh_db       [-36.0 .. 0.0 dB, default: -18.0]\n   Compression threshold (with automatic loudness-compensated makeup gain).\n\n3. ratio_mode      [2.0 .. 10.0, default: 4.0]\n   Compression ratio (2:1 to 10:1); simultaneously narrows knee curvature at\n   higher ratios as in the SSL G384 hardware (DAFx-2026 Sec. 3).\n\n4. attack_ms       [0.1 .. 30.0 ms, default: 10.0]\n   Sidechain VCA attack time constant (0.1 ms fast clamp to 30 ms punchy snap).\n\n5. release_s       [0.05 .. 1.5 s, default: 0.30]\n   Manual single-pole release time constant when auto_release is 0.\n\n6. auto_release    [0.0 .. 1.0, default: 0.65]\n   Blends in the SSL two-pole dual-RC AUTO release filter (75 ms fast transient\n   recovery pole coupled to a 1.25 s slow program-sustained recovery pole).\n\n7. sc_hpf_hz       [20.0 .. 350.0 Hz, default: 85.0]\n   Sidechain high-pass filter cutoff to prevent sub-bass energy from triggering\n   excessive full-mix pumping.\n\n8. vca_harmonics   [0.0 .. 1.0, default: 0.35]\n   THAT 202 audio VCA odd/even harmonic saturation modulated by control voltage.\n\n9. mix             [0.0 .. 1.0, default: 1.0]\n   Dry/wet parallel bus compression blend.\n\n10. output_gain_db [-24.0 .. +36.0 dB, default: 0.0]\n   Output trim, a plain gain stage after the sidechain tap and the dry/wet\n   blend, so it makes the effect up or down in level without feeding back into\n   the detector.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
